---
const startOptions = ['Start blank', 'Duplicate an existing recipe', 'Import a supported file'];
---

<section id="catalog" class="container-page py-section" aria-labelledby="catalog-heading">
	<div class="grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[5fr_6fr] lg:gap-16">
		<div data-reveal>
			<h2 id="catalog-heading" class="text-h2 font-semibold">A sauce can stay one recipe, even when it lives in five dishes.</h2>
			<p class="mt-5 max-w-[60ch] text-lede text-ink-soft">
				Ingredients hold the buying facts. Sub-recipes hold reusable batches. Dishes combine
				them. Menus define what each guest receives. Change a shared fact once and its live
				consumers recalculate.
			</p>
			<ul role="list" class="mt-7 space-y-3 text-ink-soft">
				{
					startOptions.map((option) => (
						<li class="flex items-center gap-3">
							<span class="size-1.5 shrink-0 rotate-45 bg-amber-deep" aria-hidden="true" />
							<span>{option}</span>
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ul>
			<p class="mt-6 max-w-[60ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
				Imported matches are suggestions until you approve them. Missing prices or
				conversions remain visible problems instead of becoming zero-cost ingredients.
			</p>
		</div>

		<figure data-reveal>
			<picture>
				<source media="(max-width: 639px)" srcset="/proof/yield-lines-mobile.png" />
				<img
					src="/proof/yield-lines.png"
					alt="A CostCook recipe table showing each ingredient's amount used, yield, amount to buy, preparation note, and cost contribution."
					width="1964"
					height="988"
					loading="lazy"
					decoding="async"
					class="h-auto w-full bg-paper shadow-ticket"
				/>
			</picture>
			<figcaption class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-soft">
				Used, yield, and bought stay on the same recipe line, beside the cost they produce.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</div>
</section>
